": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: bash]\nDelegating the members test investigation to a subagent while I look at the rest.\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: task]\n[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: todowrite]\nThe whole suite now passes: `python3 -m unittest` ran 16 tests, all OK. The count went from 15 to 16 because `test_search` couldn't be imported before, which counted as one error; now its two real tests run.\n\nI tracked the work with the todo list. A subagent looked into the `test_members` failures, found the cause and suggested the fix, which I applied. I fixed the other files directly; no tests were changed.\n\n| File | Problem | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| `catalog/books.py` | `parse_book` stored the year as text, which also broke `age()` | Convert it with `int(year)` |\n| `catalog/factory.py` | Sample data had only Dune and 1984 | Added the missing `Emma` book |\n| `catalog/fees.py` | Fee was days late *plus* the daily rate | Changed it to days late *times* the rate |\n| `catalog/inventory.py` | `recent(n)` returned n+1 events (`[-n-1:]`) | Now returns `[-n:]` |\n| `catalog/members.py` | `MAX_BORROWED = 3`, but the comment and tests say five | Set it to `5` |\n| `catalog/search.py` | Imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist (`catalog.nonexistent`) | Import it from `catalog.text` |\n\nOne change goes beyond what the tests check: `recent(n)` now returns an empty list when `n` is 0 or less. Without that guard, `recent(0)` would return the whole history.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 87625, "requests_cache_write": 70372, "requests_cost_usd": 0.444733, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 22, "requests_output": 3763, "reread": fa